    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d660">

                <pb facs="0769" n="667" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg667"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.119/421: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-10T15:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10, 1919,
                                3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6.50
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your December 6, 4 p.m. My telegram April 5, 4 p.m. As the Japanese Minister has
                    finally indicated that his Government would <pb facs="0770" n="668"
                        xml:id="pg668"/> agree to a declaration against the import of arms and
                    ammunition as suggested by you originally, the representatives of the five
                    powers (Italy, Japan subject to detailed authorization) have decided to make a
                    statement to the following effect, which the minister[s] of other countries here
                    represented will be invited to join.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“The Governments here represented agree effectively to restrain their
                        citizens and subjects from importing into China arms and ammunition until
                        the establishment of a government whose authority is recognized throughout
                        the country; and the Governments agree to prohibit also the importation of
                        arms contracted for but not delivered during the above named period.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>As this action is the result of the American initiative and is in itself highly
                    desirable I beg to request authorization.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
